I agree.

Some things in NetHack have an automatic, instant, and remaining reward,
giving you a unique ability that you keep for the rest of the game.

Killing your first floating eye that leave a corpse is usually the first
of these occations, granting you telepathy.

Solving Sokoban is often the second, giving you a bag of holding or amulet
of reflection.

Getting your first unicorn killed is often the third, effectively assuring
that your stats won't drop anymore.

Reaching the bottom of the Mines and retrieving the luckstone comes next,
and assures that your luck won't drop anymore, barring your own errors.

I guess all these things might be considered "mini-quests", that you have
to solve so descending deeper won't be too dangerous. Getting poison
resistance is another one, but that isn't tied to a single object or
creature.


